From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:02:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] amdv: keep the current output when the policy changes to
 force

The forced output mode only changes when userspace writes a mode, so
it keeps what an earlier forced session left. Userspace sets the force
policy and the mode in two writes. A vsync between them applies the
stale mode, and a Dolby Vision output leaves its mode for a frame or
more before the requested mode arrives.
---
 drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
@@ -0,6 +0,10 @@
 
 void set_amdv_policy(int policy)
 {
+	/* keep the current output until userspace writes a forced mode */
+	if (policy == AMDV_FORCE_OUTPUT_MODE &&
+	    dolby_vision_policy != AMDV_FORCE_OUTPUT_MODE)
+		force_mode = dolby_vision_mode;
 	dolby_vision_policy = policy;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(set_amdv_policy);
